      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14224552/assets/de81dfe9ea7efd41a7ca5b576452c62491ab438dbb0b75eb7c7a6c13a903fe6f.png)\n\nDetermine the cosine of $∠Q.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall the definition of cosine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡Q=\\frac{\\text{adjacent}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}=\\frac{QR}{PQ}=\\frac{QR}{8.5}\n$$\n\nHere, we need to determine the missing side $QR.$ The trick is to use the Pythagorean Theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}QR & =\\sqrt{P{Q}^{2}-P{R}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(8.5)^{2}-(7.5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{72.25-56.25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡Q & =\\frac{QR}{8.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{8.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{85} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{17}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
